Argentum documentation licence
================================

The **prose documentation** in this directory tree (`docs/**`) — design
records, reference material, guides, and the documentation pages of the
project website — is licensed under the **Creative Commons Attribution
4.0 International licence (CC BY 4.0)**.

    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

You may share and adapt it for any purpose, including commercially,
provided you give appropriate credit, link to the licence, and indicate
if changes were made.

Suggested attribution: *"Argentum documentation, by the Argentum project
contributors, licensed CC BY 4.0"*, with a link to
<https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>.

Code is not documentation
-------------------------

Source code, build files, and the code-sample files the documentation
embeds (`docs/uikit/snippets/**`) are under the repository's **software
licence — MIT** (see `../LICENSE`), *not* CC BY 4.0. Code that readers
copy into their own programs should carry the licence they expect.

Third-party material
--------------------

Text quoted or reproduced from other projects keeps its original licence
and copyright, with its notices kept alongside it. CC BY 4.0 applies to
this project's own prose, not to material it borrows.

Relationship to the repository's MIT grant
------------------------------------------

The repository's MIT licence (`../LICENSE`) is written to cover "the
Software and associated documentation files", so it already reaches
these documents. Nothing here revokes that: where the MIT grant applies
to a document, you may rely on **either** licence. For documentation
prose specifically, **CC BY 4.0 is the intended, stated licence**.

Why CC BY 4.0
-------------

It is a permissive documentation licence — attribution only, no
copyleft, no restriction on commercial use or on modification — and its
attribution requirement matches how this project already works (the
credits and lineage page names Fiwix and the upstream projects whose
work is adopted).

Excluded by the project's permissive-only rule, and therefore not used
here: copyleft documentation licences (CC BY-SA, GFDL), the
non-commercial variants (CC BY-NC\*), and the no-derivatives variants
(CC BY-ND\*).
